      "text": "First, let's calculate the volume of each cube. The volume \\( V \\) of a cube with edge length \\( s \\) is given by the formula:\n\\[ V = s^3 \\]\n\nThe edge length of the first cube is 6 inches. Therefore, its volume is:\n\\[ V_1 = 6^3 = 6 \\times 6 \\times 6 = 216 \\text{ cubic inches} \\]\n\nNext, we need to find the volume of the second cube. The edge length of the second cube is 1 foot. Since there are 12 inches in a foot, the edge length in inches is \\( 12 \\) inches. Therefore, its volume is:\n\\[ V_2 = 12^3 = 12 \\times 12 \\times 12 = 1728 \\text{ cubic inches} \\]\n\nNow, we need to find the ratio of the volume of the first cube to the volume of the second cube. This ratio is given by:\n\\[ \\text{Ratio} = \\frac{V_1}{V_2} = \\frac{216}{1728} \\]\n\nTo simplify this fraction, we find the greatest common divisor (GCD) of 216 and 1728. The prime factorization of 216 is:\n\\[ 216 = 2^3 \\times 3^3 \\]\n\nThe prime factorization of 1728 is:\n\\[ 1728 = 2^6 \\times 3^3 \\]\n\nThe GCD of 216 and 1728 is \\( 2^3 \\times 3^3 = 8 \\times 27 = 216 \\).\n\nWe divide both the numerator and the denominator of the fraction by their GCD, which is 216:\n\\[ \\frac{216}{1728} = \\frac{216 \\div 216}{1728 \\div 216} = \\frac{1}{8} \\]\n\nTherefore, the ratio of the volume of the cube with edge length six inches to the volume of the cube with edge length one foot is:\n\\[ \\boxed{\\frac{1}{8}} \\]",
