      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the ratio of the volume of a cube with edge length six inches to the volume of a cube with edge length one foot, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the volume of the first cube.\n2. Calculate the volume of the second cube.\n3. Find the ratio of the two volumes.\n\nFirst, let's calculate the volume of the cube with edge length six inches. The volume \\( V_1 \\) of a cube is given by the formula:\n\\[\nV_1 = \\text{edge length}^3 = 6^3 = 6 \\times 6 \\times 6 = 216 \\text{ cubic inches}\n\\]\n\nNext, let's calculate the volume of the cube with edge length one foot. Since one foot is equal to 12 inches, the edge length is 12 inches. The volume \\( V_2 \\) of this cube is:\n\\[\nV_2 = \\text{edge length}^3 = 12^3 = 12 \\times 12 \\times 12 = 1728 \\text{ cubic inches}\n\\]\n\nNow, we find the ratio of the volume of the first cube to the volume of the second cube:\n\\[\n\\text{Ratio} = \\frac{V_1}{V_2} = \\frac{216}{1728}\n\\]\n\nTo simplify this fraction, we need to find the greatest common divisor (GCD) of 216 and 1728. We can do this by finding the prime factorizations:\n\\[\n216 = 2^3 \\times 3^3\n\\]\n\\[\n1728 = 2^6 \\times 3^3\n\\]\n\nThe GCD is the product of the lowest powers of the common prime factors, which is \\( 2^3 \\times 3^3 = 8 \\times 27 = 216 \\). We divide both the numerator and the denominator of the fraction by 216:\n\\[\n\\frac{216}{1728} = \\frac{216 \\div 216}{1728 \\div 216} = \\frac{1}{8}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the ratio of the volume of the cube with edge length six inches to the volume of the cube with edge length one foot is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{1}{8}}\n\\]",
